# Page paths whose difference comes from the toolkit drawing native form
# controls, which no font decision reaches. Passed to compare_pages.sh with
# --accept, or named by an `accept` line in a plan.
#
# An accepted cell is still captured, compared and printed, marked `accepted`.
# It stays out of the worst-channel figure and the wedge heuristics and is
# counted on its own line, so it still reports when it starts matching and
# when its difference changes.
#
# The cells below differ on solid control edges at a max channel difference of
# 255. GTK draws the control on Linux and the Windows theme draws it on
# Windows.
#
# Two rules for an entry. Keep a pattern as tight as the class it names: the
# glob is matched with `case`, whose * crosses a slash, so a directory pattern
# covers everything under it and can mark a cell that broke for an unrelated
# reason. And never list a cell whose difference fails to repeat, since an
# accepted cell no longer reports a new kind of failure; fix the flake.
wt/external/wpt/css/css-writing-modes/forms/*
